meta {
  name: initialise social profile by current user
  type: http
  seq: 18
}
post {
  url: {{SUPABASE_URL}}/rest/v1/rpc/initialise_social_profile_by_current_user
  body: json
  auth: none
}
headers {
  apikey: {{SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept-Profile: api
  Content-Profile: api
}
body:json {
  {}
}
docs {
  One-time mutation, normally called by the verified OAuth callback before onboarding.
  Uses the current user's most recently used non-email/phone Auth identity; accepts no identity or metadata arguments.
  Seeds blank names on an untouched profile, without inventing a surname for a single-word name.
  Existing edited profiles are preserved. Username, privacy and product fields are unchanged.
  HTTP 200 returns null when no image import is needed, or {"provider":"google","avatar_url":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/example"} for one pending image attempt.
  Repeated calls return null. The private import marker survives avatar removal and subsequent logins.
  The application validates provider image hosts, downloads a bounded image, invokes process-image-upload with target profile_avatar, then calls complete_social_avatar_by_current_user.
  Missing images, unsupported hosts and download/processing failures do not prevent sign-in. No provider credentials are required.
  Anonymous/unauthenticated requests are rejected (42501; HTTP 403 for an authenticated anonymous session, 401 without authentication).
  Profile reads, completion configuration, billing and MFA contracts remain unchanged. REQUIRED controls completeness, not mandatory form visitation.
}
